A||||9||Carrolles||Radio cutting out||||8||
Z||000000||Carrolles||02-21-2000||01:43 PM||||I have the standard am/fm cassette player in my 85SE.  As I'm listening to the radio it will go to complete static all of the sudden.  A light tap on the console clears it up most of the time.  The clock loses time also.<P>I've had it out and checked all the wire connectors, grounds, antenna ground, and I even opened up the radio looking for loose wires or cold solder joints.  I'd rather keep the original radio to keep the car stock but I'm about ready to give up.<P>Has anyone else had this happen?  I had a similar problem with this same type radio in an 86 Olds Calais.  The car got totaled before I was able to try and fix the radio.<P>TIA,<P>Carroll||||reg||8
Z||000001||William Federle||02-21-2000||07:07 PM||||Something like that happened to me recently. It turned out to be a wire in the black plug (the bottom one of three plugs in the rear-left of the radio). The wire in the hole for pin F was loose and wouldn't stay in. The tang that holds it in the plug was broken off. I stuck it back in and used RTV on it and the other wires going into that plug and let it cure for 24 hrs. Problem gone. (I looked around to find a replacement plug but only the other gender plug is available at Radio Shack or the auto parts stores).<BR><p>[This message has been edited by William Federle (edited 02-21-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||theogre||02-21-2000||07:11 PM||||check the main and antena plugs. someone may have yanked the antena working under the dash. after that it might be the radio has a loose wire inside.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Brian84SE||02-21-2000||08:14 PM||||The exact same thing is happening to me in my  84SE with the factory am/fm/cassette.  I just recently got the car so I havent had it out yet.  Hitting the side doesnt seem to help though.  It just comes back in on its own.  Usually under a minute.  If you figure out what it was please let me know.  I love the sound of the stereo but it's getting anoying!||||reg||1
Z||000004||Carrolles||02-22-2000||11:47 PM||||It used to take a pretty hard whack on the side to get it to start up again.  I found that a gentle tap on top of the radio surround bezel works fine.<P>I'll check out the wiring plug soon.<P>Thanks,<P>Carroll||||reg||1
